<section class="slide s-big-list s-discuss" id="discuss" data-part="Discussion">
  <p class="kicker">Reflection</p>
  <h2>Discuss with your table</h2>
  <ol class="share">
    <li>What are the advantages of writing grammar rules as ordinary Python functions rather than creating a domain-specific frameworks?</li>
    <li>How could box splitting be applied to handle connected structures like roads, bridges, and walls?</li>
    <li>Where else in procedural generation could Box-Split Grammars be applied?</li>
  </ol>
  <aside class="notes">Open discussion questions encouraging participants to analyze the trade-offs of Python-embedded grammars and general procedural content generation challenges.</aside>
</section>
